      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** If you really want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting the override.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
